  <body>
    <outline text="November 2026" type="calendarMonth" date="2026-11">
      <outline text="21st November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-21">
        <outline text="![Loch Lomond](/images/2026/11/000009360001-21201545.webp)" created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:15:14 GMT"/>
        <outline text="A new fountain pen 🖋️" created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:31:29 GMT">
          <outline text="Instead of debating endlessly for a week or more, I just went ahead and ordered one, plus some de atramentis document ink for it. Because that's what the lady said she used and it looked good. " created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:51:11 GMT"/>
          <outline text="I'm not sure what the behaviour is if I nest this under an image? Also I don't think the site CSS does much with very deep nestings. At some point I'd like some to actually be a bullet list but not sure how I should trigger that? Perhaps an option in the parent node? "/>
          <outline text="Buying this pen triggered getting a 15% off voucher...maybe I need a mechanical pencil..." created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:57:55 GMT"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Porridge updates 🥣" created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:20:18 GMT">
          <outline text="You can add bullets now. Click on the parent bullet menu. A little pill appears on the parent row in the editor so you know." created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:20:29 GMT" list="bullets">
            <outline text="We're all children"/>
            <outline text="I'm the favourite"/>
            <outline text="No, I am."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Added a button in the menu to open your rendered blog from the editor"/>
          <outline text="New domain - The editor is now &lt;https://porridge.alexjj.com&gt;">
            <outline text=" btw if you want a custom domain, add it under the Github repo Pages settings, then update the blog settings via the editor."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="20th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-20">
        <outline text="![A Dreich Driesh](/images/2026/11/000004210035-20084123.webp)" created="Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:40:13 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Waiting for the plumber to come and fix two water leaks...this is also before he continues working on the bathroom that's been out of action for the week. Least he's coming." created="Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:28:18 GMT"/>
        <outline text="It means a day at home, without work, and not going hill walking - which is a shame as it's a lovely day, cold but blue skies and sunny. Probably there are things I can be doing to fix stuff or plan christmas etc. Do indoor things that I put off. This also risks sitting on the computer and achieving nothing...which is one reason why I like to go out, at least I achieve something and not just waste away the day" created="Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:28:59 GMT"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="18th November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-18">
        <outline text="Porridge 🥣" created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:26:18 GMT">
          <outline text="Probably a terrible name but it just popped into my head. This is a blogging engine heavily inspired by drummer and dynalist. Everything is an outline and static files. Right now it's all built and running on Github repo, actions and pages. The intent is that there's nothing to host and it's fairly straight forward for others to host." created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:26:32 GMT"/>
          <outline text="There's the main [app repo](https://github.com/alexjj/porridge), which runs the [interface](https://alexjj.github.io/porridge/), a [blog template](https://github.com/alexjj/porridge-blog-template) repo which you use to start off your blog." created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:17:55 GMT"/>
          <outline text="You link the app to your git repo using a fine-grained token (maybe I'll make a &quot;sign in with Github&quot; thing later) - this is just saved in your browser's local storage - and then the app can commit to your repo. Your repo has a github action in it which will build your blog and then be hosted on github pages (assuming you've turned that on). " created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:17:56 GMT"/>
          <outline text="More instructions will come / are in the readme." created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:17:57 GMT"/>
          <outline text="It *should* work nicely on your phone as well..." created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:17:58 GMT"/>
          <outline text="Oh and Claude code built all of this...if that matters." created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:17:59 GMT"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="![a big stack of notebooks](/images/2026/11/notebooks-18201150.jpg)" created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:08:28 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Here we are. The first test entry on this new blogging system (not copied, honestly...)" created="Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:45:38 GMT"/>
      </outline>
    </outline>
  </body>
</opml>
